  "Question": "What is the inradius of a right triangle with legs 3 and 4?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The hypotenuse is 5. The inradius of a right triangle is \\(r=(a+b-c)/2=(3+4-5)/2=1\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the inradius as a common height\n\nJoining the incenter to the three vertices divides the triangle into three smaller triangles. Their heights to the original sides all equal the inradius \\(r\\), which lets us express the whole area in terms of \\(r\\). The hypotenuse is \\(\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=5\\), so\n\\[\n\\frac{3\\times4}{2}=\\frac{3r}{2}+\\frac{4r}{2}+\\frac{5r}{2}=6r.\n\\]\nThus \\(6=6r\\), and the inradius is \\(r=1\\).",
